# Resource Limits

Do not exhaust host RAM when testing, building, checking, or running the stack.

## Prefer just recipes

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Backend unit tests | `just test` |
| Frontend type check | `just check` |
| Rebuild harness images | `just build-harness` |
| Start harness (no rebuild) | `just up-harness-fast` |
| Start harness (rebuild) | `just up-harness` |

## Rules

- **Never** run two RAM-heavy tasks concurrently (e.g. `just baseline` + `docker compose build` + `bun run check`).
- Build harness images **one service at a time** — backend, then frontend (`just build-harness`).
- Use `just up-harness-fast` when images are already current (avoids Docker Hub pulls).
- Run pytest **inside** the harness container (`just test`), not host `python -m pytest` without a venv.
- Do **not** add `pytest-xdist` or multi-worker pytest — keep single-process.
- Do **not** weaken or skip compatibility checks to save RAM — serialize work instead.

## Overrides

Tune via env vars (see `scripts/lib/resources.sh`):

- `COMPOSE_PARALLEL_LIMIT` (default `1`)
- `NODE_MAX_OLD_SPACE_SIZE` (default `2048`)
- `BUILDKIT_STEP_MAX_CONCURRENCY` (default `1`)
